{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034591-arete-rolls-and-possession","id":1034591,"title":"Arete rolls and possession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T07:38:04-08:00","id":1034591,"title":"Arete rolls and possession","content":"Let's say someone with spirit four allows a spirit to possess him for awhile, M20 clearly says that person cannot use the spirits charms, so what exactly can the possessed individual harness from the spirit? And, would you roll ar\u00eate to utilize that power, since you are cut off from &quot;true magick&quot; according to spirit 3's description","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:35:01-08:00","id":1034621,"title":"","content":"In older editions you could use the Charms but lost access to Magick while possessed. Our group still goes by these rules. Without access to Charms being possessed by a spirit loses most of its usefulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:23:09-08:00","id":1034737,"title":"","content":"Well, ideally, you get yourself possessed by a spirit that has something useful in a less mechanical sense under these rules. It makes purposeful possession much more about channeling powerful entities to become a font for their knowledge, insights, etc. than getting access to a bunch of Paradox free powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:19:37-08:00","id":1034774,"title":"","content":"Under M20 rules, Charms are out of the question, but Abilities are not. This can be helpful if, for instance, you have a character with no combat experience channel a spirit of war, so as to tap the spirit's Brawl Talent, Melee Skill, and Academics (Strategy) Knowledge. Granted, a war spirit is going to be harder to approach for this character, since they embody few of the qualities such an Umbrood can identify with. But simply the chance to facilitate combat in the material world could be enticement enough, provided the Mage makes an adequate social roll during negotiation.<br /> <br /> Still, I agree with Tuch, insomuch as not being able to channel a spirit's Charms makes possession much less appealing. Given the risks involved in self-possession, it doesn't seem as worth the trouble, unless the spirit has high scores in Abilities the Mage desperately needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}